 result←object Reset arg;wins;pool;cleanup
⍝ Reset the entire GUI state immediately

 '∆WI ACTION ERROR: Method "Reset" does not accept an argument'##.##.Error×≢arg

 :If ×≢wins←object ##.children ⍬ ⍝ What are the top-level objects?
     wins ##.##.∆WI¨⊂'*Delete' ⍝ Delete each top-level object in the usual way, by GUI name (allow UDC customization)
 :EndIf
 :If ⎕NULL≠pool←##.##.GUIroot ⎕VGET⊂'_Pool'⎕NULL ⍝ Clean out _Pool object cross-references first
     pool←2⊃pool ⎕VGET 9 ⍝ Get a list of object references currently in the pool
     :For cleanup :In ⎕NULL~⍨pool ⎕VGET⊂'∆EX'⎕NULL ⋄ ##.##.∆EX⍕cleanup ⋄ :EndFor ⍝ Look for any ∆EX: references to clean up first
 :EndIf
 ⍝ Throw away the system object and all its contents, too - they'll be recreated with default values on the next call
 ##.##.∆EX⍕##.##.GUIroot
⍝? When we're using EWC, how do we kill off all the root properties?
 ##.##.Application.⎕EX'∆WSELF' '∆WEVENT' '∆WARG' '∆WRES' ⍝ Dispose of all the ∆W-variables
 result←##.NoRes
